-- The other direction: a missing field that must NOT eliminate rows. Every other missing-field step here returns
-- empty, so a bug that made these predicates over-eliminate would look identical to correct behaviour. IS MISSING is
-- true for a field the table does not have, so this must return exactly what "bucket < 3" alone returns.
-- The predicate is still dropped from the pushed filter (unbindable), which is precisely why it has to be evaluated
-- correctly on the rows.
SELECT id
FROM variantPredicateShapes
WHERE variant_field.bucket < 3 AND nosuchcolumn IS MISSING
ORDER BY id;
